      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALDEBARAN ABEL (10) was unplaced two starts ago then things went amiss last start when he broke and finished 10 metres away in eighth over 1720m at this track. Will need an ounce of luck to slot in from this tricky draw. Meets a similar line up so he is sure to be a force if the manners improve. CARLA PIXIE NZ (8) continued her impressive run of recent efforts last time out when runner-up over 1720m at this track, beaten 8 metres. Can settle just behind them and wait on the sprint lane. Has the ability to take this out. KYVALLEY MICHAEL NZ (3) missed the placings two runs back then did a great job to finish 8 metres back in third despite breaking in the run over 2240m at this track two weeks ago. A nice draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Meets a similar line up so he must be considered. SKY FLAIR (2) is the best of the rest after finishing runner-up when resuming over 2240m at this track last time out.",
